    {"type": "Texture", "tag": "HS3hr/MH1, _", "duration": 4, "line": "top.3", "start": 396, "comment": " r ou non ?"},
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 4,
      "comment": "FL : maybe cut the bar? H6h, M1/M1 ?\nLC : I thought first half was too short... but it is true that the cut is neat ; to discuss and confirm. I have new doubts about the decomposition (H4h/S2o) which may be unnecessary.\nconsensus : change from 2[H6h_(H4h/S2o)/M1/M1_] to H6h, M1/M1"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 12,
      "comment": "FL: maybe cut the bar? H6h, M1/M1 ?\nLC : potentialy : see m.2\nconsensus : see m.2 Change from 2[H6h_(H4h/S2o)/M1/M1_] to H6h, M1/M1"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 36,
      "comment": "FL: why h for the global? (homorhythmy is not exact, it's nearly more p than h, it's more heterophony\nLC : I considered some kind of appoggiatura/grace note (but it is probably overinterpreted). If there is no homorhythmy, we cannot annotate 'p' either (even if a parallel voice is hidden, yes). Proposition : M1/MH2h\nconsensus : change from 3h[M1/MH2h] to M1/MH2h"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 44,
      "comment": "FL: as in bar 10: why h for the global? (homorhythmy is not exact, it's nearly more p than h, it's more heterophony\nLC : same as m.10 : proposition : M1/MH2h, MH3h/S1\nconsensus : see m.10 : change from 3h[M1/MH2h], MH3h/S1 to M1/MH2h, MH3h/S1"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 52,
      "comment": "FL:in MH2p/S1, S1 is debattable... only one note: S1_ ? nothing? or keep the continuation of the previous bar?\nLC : S1 for continuity, yes. I agree the note is short here (even if sequential separation often replace '_' by considering shorter sections). Change : MH2p/S1, M1s/MS1(M1/S1) to MH2p/S1_, M1s/MS1(M1/S1)\nLC : reopen : parallelism ?\nconsensus : keep parallelism, keep the label"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 112,
      "comment": "FL : scale?\nLC : ambiguity with the graces notes... but I agree this definitely corresponds to the typical scale motif that we annotate. Change MH1 to MH1s."
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 132,
      "comment": "FL: Iwould cut the bar in two as in bar 32: MHS2 (maybe no s), M1s/H3h\nLC : the 's' is there because it is the third repetition of the motive exposed twice in previous bar. And I still don't understand why MHS2 there.\nconsensus : no change"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 124,
      "comment": "FL: I would cut the bar in two: MHS2, M1s/H3h\nLC : The original cut was not so obvious because it breaks a possible continuity of the upper layer. I do not understand the MHS2 : the texture is the same as previous measure, with to clearly seperated layers.\nconsensus : no change"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 140,
      "comment": "FL: why S? no repetition\nLC : same case as K280-1 m.27 : and we had a consensus on removing S. Change from M1/MS2o to M1/M2o"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 152,
      "comment": "FL: MH1s?\nLC : arpeggiated, and not neighbouring moves ('conjoints') ? Oh, it is true that it is the same as following bars ! So let's be consistent : change from H3h/S1, MH1 to H3h/S1, MH1s"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 156,
      "comment": "FL: MH1s?\nLC : same as previous measure. Change from H3h/S1, MH1 to H3h/S1, MH1s"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 176,
      "comment": "FL: MS1s (S1/M1s) (twice) ?\nLC : the note that is kept bothers me a little. The nested 'M1' layer could eventually have 's' (but the upper 'S1' would be close to 'r', which is debatable because it is more alternation that \"real\" repetition)\nconsensus : change from MS1(S1/M1)/M2o, M1/MS1(S1/M1) to MS1s(S1/M1s)/M2o, M1/MS1s (S1/M1s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 180,
      "comment": "FL: MS1s (S1/M1s) (twice) ?\nLC : to discuss.\nconsensus : change from MS1(S1/M1)/M1, M1/MS1(S1/M1) to MS1s(S1/M1s)/M1, M1/MS1s (S1/M1s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 184,
      "comment": "FL: MS1s (S1/M1s), M1s\nLC : to discuss.\nconsensus : change from MS1(S1/M1)/M1, M1 to MS1s(S1/M1s), M1"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 200,
      "comment": "FL: M1s/S2o_ for the second part?\nLC : yes. Change from  M1/HS1(S1/M1), M1/S2o_ to M1/HS1(S1/M1), M1s/S2o_"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 216,
      "comment": "FL: MH1/S1_ for the second part?\nLC : too short arpeggio ; and it would be H in following measure too ?\nconsensus : no change"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 232,
      "comment": "FL: cut the bar? H6h, M1/M1_\nLC : to discuss. Partly agree on the separation ; also need to confirm decomposition (H4h/S2o)\nconsensus : see m.2, change from 2[H6h_(H4h/S2o)/M1/M1_] to H6h, M1/M1"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 240,
      "comment": "FL: cut the bar? H6h, M1/M1_\nLC: same as bar 59\nconsensus : consensus : change from 2[H6h_(H4h/S2o)/M1/M1_] to H6h, M1/M1"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 264,
      "comment": "FL: seems too complicated... M1/HS1(S1/M1), H3h/S1 ? (can we cut not strictly in the middle?)\nLC: the H3h seems really short to be indicated this way. But I also agree that H2_ is overly complicated/verbose. What about 2[H3h/S1] for the end ?\nconsensus : change from M1/HS1(S1/M1), 3[H2h_/M1/S1] to M1/HS1(S1/M1), 3[MH3h/S1]"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 268,
      "comment": "FL: p or h?\nLC: at least h, and there is only the C which is not in pure parallelism. I think it is negligible andwe can fully consider it are dominant parallel motions. To confirm.\nconsensus : keep label"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 272,
      "comment": "FL: global density 2? p or h?\nLC: agree for density 2. Same argument as previously for parallelism. It strongly appears to me as parallel. Proposition : 2[MH2p/S1_], _\nconsensus : change to 2[MH2p/S1_], _ (p to confirm)\nconsensus : keep label"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 336,
      "comment": "FL: global density useless? 1+1=2\nLC : always better to indicate it when there is a sparse layer, by precaution."
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 356,
      "comment": "FL: scale?\nLC : yes, as bar 29 : change MH1 to MH1s"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 384,
      "comment": "FL: why S?\nLC : true, same as consensus on K280-1 and bar 36 in this movement. Change M1/MS2o to M1/M2o"
    },
    {
      "type": "Positive Feedback",
      "tag": "doubt",
      "duration": 4,
      "line": "top.2",
      "start": 48,
      "comment": "LC : parallelism ? cf next measure.\nconsensus : keep parallelism"
